  "source_detail": "PLAN.md Q1 — how an agent names a group and marks the words pointing at it",
  "explanation": "Both routes end at the same place: boxes light up. What differs is whether the group has a name of its own. Follow the right-hand route and one entry holds the ids, so a second mention points at the same name and the server can refuse a name that resolves to nothing. Follow the left and the ids live inside each sentence, so a second mention restates them and nothing catches the two drifting apart. Leaves out the markup itself — the words in the prose get marked the same way either way.",
